    <chapter xml:id="chap-multiverses">
      <title>Multiverses (40 min)</title>
      <introduction>
        <assemblage component="TODO">
          <title>Check time</title>
          <p>EAJ, 3Aug2026</p>
          <p>TG overview slide 3 says this is 40min, but slide 9 says 35min. Which one is correct?</p>
        </assemblage>
        <p>In this part, students learn about logical puzzles, tables to represent solutions, and the notion of a <term>world</term> (an object or possible configuration in a combinatorial situation). By creating and counting worlds, and extending and solving puzzles, students develop mathematical skills related to modelling, counting and reasoning with logic.</p>

        <p>The combinatorial situation will allow for cultural exchanges related to hobbies. It will also make students more aware about biases or stereotypes that people has when thinking about hobbies based on gender. By connecting to the combinatorial idea of multiple worlds, and the idea of using logic and not just guessing, students can discuss how math can help reduce stereotypes.</p>

        <p>Students will learn about permutations (in the form of tables), count them, and explore how changing parameters lead to new counting. They use tree diagrams and time strips, and make sense of multiplication equations.</p>

        <paragraphs>
          <title>Breakdown</title>
          <p>
          <dl>
            <li>
              <title><xref ref="sec-viajeros" text="type-global"/></title>
              <p><xref ref="sec-viajeros" text="title"/></p>
              <p>Students play the game-puzzle, and familiarize with the setting.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <title><xref ref="sec-amigos" text="type-global"/></title>
              <p><xref ref="sec-amigos" text="title"/></p>
              <p>Students explore ways to count the total number of options.</p>
            </li>
          </dl>
          </p>
          <assemblage component="TODO">
            <title>Check times for the breakdown</title>
            <p>The TG slide breakdown p9 lists 10min and 25mins, but they don't seem to match the following slides: Viajeros is 5 min in the Overview (slide.6) and activity header (slide.10) but 10 min in the Part 1 breakdown (slide.9). Cuatro Amigos is 20 min in the Overview (slide.6), 25 min in the breakdown (slide.9), and 15 min in the activity header (slide.14). The section titles currently use the Overview times (5 min / 20 min); reconcile.</p>
            <p>As authored in PreTeXt, this involves fixing the time in the activity headers, which becomes the single source of thruth to avoid these inconsistencies.</p>
          </assemblage>
        </paragraphs>

        <objectives>
          <ul>
            <li><p>Use tree diagrams to count worlds.</p></li>
          </ul>
        </objectives>

        <paragraphs>
          <title>Materials</title>
          <ul>
            <li><p>Student Workbook (<url href="https://mathceo-uci.github.io/cuatroAmigos-sw.pdf">pdf</url> / <url href="https://mathceo-uci.github.io/cuatroAmigos-workbook">web</url>)</p></li>
            <li>(large paper)</li>
            <!-- <li><p>Sets of 16 colored squares (<url href="external/cuatroAmigos-blm-coloredSquares.pdf">pdf</url>)</p></li> -->
            <li><p>Friends &amp; Hobby Cards (several sets of 8) (<url href="external/cuatroAmigos-blm-friendsHobbyCards.pdf">pdf PENDING</url>)</p></li>
            <!-- <li><p>Tally Charts (for teachers) (<url href="external/cuatroAmigos-blm-tallyChart.pdf">pdf</url>)</p></li> -->
            <li><p>Mini-tables (several copies) (<url href="external/cuatroAmigos-blm-miniTables.pdf">pdf PENDING</url>)</p></li>
            <!-- <li><p>Large Trees (2-sided) (<url href="external/cuatroAmigos-blm-largeTree.pdf">pdf</url>)</p></li> -->
            <li><p>Whiteboards and Markers</p></li>
          </ul>
